# TF-903: Fix the formatting and vet complaints in report.go

## Goal

`report.go` is not gofmt formatted and `go vet` complains about it. Fix both.
The program must behave the same.

## Dependencies

None

## Scope

Edit only `report.go`. Run gofmt on it. Fix the `Printf` call that has the
wrong number of arguments for its format string.

## Constraints

Do not edit any test. Add no dependencies. Touch only `report.go`. Commit the
change on the task branch.

## Success criteria

### C1: gofmt lists no files

Check: test -z "$(gofmt -l .)"

### C2: go vet is clean

Check: go vet ./...

### C3: The unit tests pass

Check: go test ./...

## Verification

Run each check from the repository root and report its exit code.
